IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je21-nouns`
IMPORT `je21-seat-2-powers-and-effects`
IMPORT `je21-seat-3-versions-and-publication`

-- je21-tests-independent-2: an independent test author's reading of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 (L.8/2021), asserted against the exported questions of the row. Part 2 of 2: Articles 9 to 22.
-- The first version of this file was one module of 887 lines (je21-tests-independent.l4); it was split by Article into two, and no assertion was lost: this part has 183 assertions and the other has 152, 335 in all.
-- Status: ASSUMED, NOT RULED. These are one reader's answers, decided from the text of the Law alone before any file of the encoding was opened; the owner of the Law has ruled on none of them.
-- Only the mapping of each decided answer onto an exported question (its inputs, and whether FALSE or a refusal is the answer) was made after the seat modules were read, and by the rule below, fixed before the run.
-- Where the text allows two readings and the author could not decide, the assertion is in the last section, carries "UNSURE" in its comment, and asserts the reading the author would take; a failure there is a triage item, not a verdict.
-- A failing assertion is a finding. After the first run of the whole file (335 assertions: 323 satisfied, 9 failed, 3 refused as a warning) each was triaged; the table is in NOTES.md section 10.3.
-- No expected value was edited to fit what the code answered. Four BECAUSE texts were corrected (the author's error, below), one assertion was moved to a registered alternative reading, and the rest were settled by changes to the encoding.
--
-- Citations in the comments are bare locators, "(src:N)", lines of the current text of the Law; none is a quotation, so none is a quote line.
-- Bracketed ids such as [C-01] are the author's scenario ids.
--
-- How a refusal is asserted. "#ASSERT REFUSED expr BECAUSE msg" needs msg to equal the refusal text exactly.
-- Where the refusal comes from the REFUSE written in the exported question itself, the BECAUSE text is that REFUSE copied verbatim.
-- Where the refusal can come from a rule module (not read by the author before this file was written), the assertion has no BECAUSE.
-- Author's error, corrected after the first run: four assertions on Article 9(2), 9(3) and 9(4) for legislation made on or before 28 Mar 2003 carried the BECAUSE of the exported question,
-- but the refusal that answers is raised by the rule module with a different text; each now carries the text actually raised, with a comment above it.
-- They refused, as decided; they had failed only on the message.
--
-- The author's rule for FALSE against REFUSE (fixed before the run):
--   FALSE when the Law states a limit in terms ("only if", "other than", "no later than", "limited to") or the question is whether an Article applies to something outside its stated scope;
--   a refusal when the question is whether something MAY be done, the Article gives permission only on conditions that are not met, and the Law says nothing else.
--

§ `Helpers`

-- The legislation an incidental provision would amend: form, is the Human Rights (Jersey) Law 2000, is the legislation giving the power.
GIVEN f IS A `Form of legislation`, h IS A BOOLEAN, e IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Legislation to be amended`
`ind: to amend` f h e MEANS
    `Legislation to be amended` WITH
        `its form` IS f
        `it is the Human Rights (Jersey) Law 2000` IS h
        `it is the legislation giving the power to make the instrument` IS e

-- A document: legislation of some jurisdiction, accessible without charge, concerned with a technical product, aimed at specialists.
GIVEN l IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A BOOLEAN, t IS A BOOLEAN, s IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts about a document`
`ind: a document with` l c t s MEANS
    `Facts about a document` WITH
        `it is legislation from some jurisdiction` IS l
        `it is accessible to the public without charge` IS c
        `it is concerned with the practices, procedures, processes or requirements for use of a technical product` IS t
        `it is aimed at a person with particular knowledge or experience in that technical field` IS s

-- A text: kind, Jersey legislation, carries the official-version statement, electronic version on a website under the Drafter's authority or an unaltered copy, printed version issued by or for the Drafter.
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of text under Part 3`, j IS A BOOLEAN, s IS A BOOLEAN, e IS A BOOLEAN, p IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts about a text`
`ind: a text with` k j s e p MEANS
    `Facts about a text` WITH
        `its kind` IS k
        `it is Jersey legislation` IS j
        `it contains a statement that it is an official version of the legislation issued under the authority of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021` IS s
        `it is an electronic version displayed on a website under the authority of the Principal Legislative Drafter, or a printed or downloaded copy of that without any alteration to its text or format` IS e
        `it is a printed version issued by or on behalf of the Principal Legislative Drafter` IS p

-- A provider of instructions: Member of the States, officer in a department, officer in a body or unit established on behalf of the States, otherwise gives instructions.
GIVEN m IS A BOOLEAN, d IS A BOOLEAN, b IS A BOOLEAN, o IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts about a provider of instructions`
`ind: a provider who` m d b o MEANS
    `Facts about a provider of instructions` WITH
        `is a Member of the States` IS m
        `is an officer working in a department established by the States` IS d
        `is an officer working in a body, office or unit of administration established on behalf of the States` IS b
        `otherwise provides instructions to the Legislative Drafting Office` IS o

-- A change in a draft revision relying on a power.
GIVEN w IS A STRING, a IS AN `Authority relied on for a change`
GIVETH A `Change in a draft revision`
`ind: a change` w a MEANS `Change in a draft revision` WITH `what the change does` IS w, `the authority relied on` IS a

GIVEN p IS A `Power in Schedule 1`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind: Schedule 1 power relied on` p MEANS `Is the power relied on for this change one the Law gives?` (`a power in Schedule 1` p)

§ `Article 9: powers to make subordinate legislation`

-- Art 9(1) (src:91) [I-01, I-02]: a power conferred by Jersey legislation, no provision to the contrary: used from time to time, and to repeal, amend or replace.
#ASSERT `May a power to make subordinate legislation be used again, and to repeal, amend or replace what was made?` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 9(1) [I-03]: provision to the contrary.
#ASSERT REFUSED `May a power to make subordinate legislation be used again, and to repeal, amend or replace what was made?` TRUE TRUE BECAUSE "Article 9(1) gives these incidents to a power Jersey legislation confers unless provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say what holds in any other case"
-- Art 9(1) [I-03]: a power not conferred by Jersey legislation: the Law says nothing.
#ASSERT REFUSED `May a power to make subordinate legislation be used again, and to repeal, amend or replace what was made?` FALSE FALSE BECAUSE "Article 9(1) gives these incidents to a power Jersey legislation confers unless provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say what holds in any other case"
-- Art 9(2) (src:92) [I-04]: legislation made 29 Mar 2003 (after 28 Mar 2003) confers the power: different provision for different cases.
#ASSERT `May a power to make subordinate legislation apply generally or be limited, or differ for different cases?` (YMD 2003 3 29) TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 9(2) [I-05]: legislation made on 28 Mar 2003 is not "made after 28 March 2003".
-- Corrected after the first run (the author's error): the refusal is raised by the rule module, so BECAUSE is the rule module's text (NOTES.md section 10.3).
#ASSERT REFUSED `May a power to make subordinate legislation apply generally or be limited, or differ for different cases?` (YMD 2003 3 28) TRUE FALSE BECAUSE "Article 9(2) is confined to legislation made after 28th March 2003, and the Law does not say what holds for legislation made on or before that day"
-- Art 9(2) [I-06]: legislation made 27 Mar 2003.
-- Corrected after the first run (the author's error): the refusal is raised by the rule module, so BECAUSE is the rule module's text (NOTES.md section 10.3).
#ASSERT REFUSED `May a power to make subordinate legislation apply generally or be limited, or differ for different cases?` (YMD 2003 3 27) TRUE FALSE BECAUSE "Article 9(2) is confined to legislation made after 28th March 2003, and the Law does not say what holds for legislation made on or before that day"
-- Art 9(2) [I-04]: legislation made in 2020.
#ASSERT `May a power to make subordinate legislation apply generally or be limited, or differ for different cases?` (YMD 2020 1 1) TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 9(2) [I-07]: made in 2020 with provision to the contrary.
#ASSERT REFUSED `May a power to make subordinate legislation apply generally or be limited, or differ for different cases?` (YMD 2020 1 1) TRUE TRUE BECAUSE "Article 9(2) lets a power conferred by Jersey legislation made after 28 March 2003 take these forms unless provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say what holds in any other case"
-- Art 9(3) (src:95) [I-08]: a class includes a single case: provision about one case is within Art 9(2).
#ASSERT `Is provision about this many cases within the power of Article 9(2)?` 1 (YMD 2003 3 29) TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 9(3) [I-08]: provision about three cases.
#ASSERT `Is provision about this many cases within the power of Article 9(2)?` 3 (YMD 2010 1 1) TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 9(3) [I-09]: power conferred by legislation made on 28 Mar 2003: Art 9(3) is for the purposes of Art 9(2) only.
-- Corrected after the first run (the author's error): the refusal is raised by the rule module, so BECAUSE is the rule module's text (NOTES.md section 10.3).
#ASSERT REFUSED `Is provision about this many cases within the power of Article 9(2)?` 1 (YMD 2003 3 28) TRUE FALSE BECAUSE "Article 9(2) is confined to legislation made after 28th March 2003, and the Law does not say what holds for legislation made on or before that day"
-- Art 9(4) (src:96) [I-10]: a repeal brought into force in part, power from legislation made 29 Mar 2003.
#ASSERT `May a repeal be brought into force in part?` (YMD 2003 3 29) TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 9(4) [I-11]: the same, power from legislation made 28 Mar 2003.
-- Corrected after the first run (the author's error): the refusal is raised by the rule module, so BECAUSE is the rule module's text (NOTES.md section 10.3).
#ASSERT REFUSED `May a repeal be brought into force in part?` (YMD 2003 3 28) TRUE FALSE BECAUSE "Article 9(2) is confined to legislation made after 28th March 2003, and the Law does not say what holds for legislation made on or before that day"
-- Art 9(5), 9(6)(a) (src:97, 99) [I-12]: Regulations amending a Law that is not the Human Rights (Jersey) Law 2000 and not the enabling Law: authorised.
#ASSERT `Can this instrument use the incidental power of Article 9(5) to make this provision?` `Regulations` (`ind: to amend` `a Law` FALSE FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 9(6)(a) [I-13]: Regulations amending the Human Rights (Jersey) Law 2000: barred.
#ASSERT `Can this instrument use the incidental power of Article 9(5) to make this provision?` `Regulations` (`ind: to amend` `a Law` TRUE FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 9(6)(a) [I-14]: Regulations amending the legislation giving the power: barred.
#ASSERT `Can this instrument use the incidental power of Article 9(5) to make this provision?` `Regulations` (`ind: to amend` `a Law` FALSE TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 9(6)(a) [I-15]: Regulations amending an Order: authorised.
#ASSERT `Can this instrument use the incidental power of Article 9(5) to make this provision?` `Regulations` (`ind: to amend` `an Order` FALSE FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 9(6)(a) (src:99) [I-16]: Regulations amending UK extended legislation: "any legislation other than" the two; UK extended legislation is legislation.
#ASSERT `Can this instrument use the incidental power of Article 9(5) to make this provision?` `Regulations` (`ind: to amend` `UK extended legislation` FALSE FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 9(6)(a) [V-06]: Triennial Regulations are Regulations (Art 2(3)(a)): barred from the Human Rights (Jersey) Law 2000.
#ASSERT `Can this instrument use the incidental power of Article 9(5) to make this provision?` `Triennial Regulations` (`ind: to amend` `a Law` TRUE FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 9(6)(b) (src:100) [I-18]: an Order of a Minister amending a Law (made by the States): barred.
#ASSERT `Can this instrument use the incidental power of Article 9(5) to make this provision?` `an Order` (`ind: to amend` `a Law` FALSE FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 9(6)(b) [I-19]: an Order amending Regulations (made by the States): barred.
#ASSERT `Can this instrument use the incidental power of Article 9(5) to make this provision?` `an Order` (`ind: to amend` `Regulations` FALSE FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 9(6)(b) [I-20]: an Order amending another Order (not made by the States): authorised.
#ASSERT `Can this instrument use the incidental power of Article 9(5) to make this provision?` `an Order` (`ind: to amend` `an Order` FALSE FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 9(6)(b) [I-22]: an Order amending the Human Rights (Jersey) Law 2000: barred (it is a Law).
#ASSERT `Can this instrument use the incidental power of Article 9(5) to make this provision?` `an Order` (`ind: to amend` `a Law` TRUE FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 9(6)(b) [I-23]: an Order amending the Law that gives the power: barred (it is a Law).
#ASSERT `Can this instrument use the incidental power of Article 9(5) to make this provision?` `an Order` (`ind: to amend` `a Law` FALSE TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 9(6)(b) [I-18]: another instrument having legislative effect in Jersey amending a Law: barred.
#ASSERT `Can this instrument use the incidental power of Article 9(5) to make this provision?` `another instrument having legislative effect in Jersey` (`ind: to amend` `a Law` FALSE FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 9(6)(b) [I-20]: another such instrument amending an Order: authorised.
#ASSERT `Can this instrument use the incidental power of Article 9(5) to make this provision?` `another instrument having legislative effect in Jersey` (`ind: to amend` `an Order` FALSE FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 9(5) (src:97) [I-17]: Regulations with provision to the contrary: Art 9(5) gives nothing; what the contrary provision does is not in this Law.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Can this instrument use the incidental power of Article 9(5) to make this provision?` `Regulations` (`ind: to amend` `a Law` FALSE FALSE) TRUE TRUE BECAUSE "Article 9(5) gives the incidental power unless provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say what the contrary provision does instead"
-- Art 9(5) [I-25]: an Order with provision to the contrary.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Can this instrument use the incidental power of Article 9(5) to make this provision?` `an Order` (`ind: to amend` `a Law` FALSE FALSE) TRUE TRUE BECAUSE "Article 9(5) gives the incidental power unless provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say what the contrary provision does instead"
-- Art 9(5) [I-25]: an Order with provision to the contrary, amending another Order.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Can this instrument use the incidental power of Article 9(5) to make this provision?` `an Order` (`ind: to amend` `an Order` FALSE FALSE) TRUE TRUE BECAUSE "Article 9(5) gives the incidental power unless provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say what the contrary provision does instead"
-- Art 9(7) (src:101) [I-28, I-31]: stated to be made under a power, and may be made under this power: treated as made under it.
#ASSERT `Is this subordinate legislation treated as made under this power?` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 9(7) [I-29]: no power stated: Art 9(7) does not apply; the Law says nothing.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Is this subordinate legislation treated as made under this power?` FALSE TRUE BECAUSE "Article 9(7) treats subordinate legislation as made under a power when it says it is made under a power conferred by legislation and may be made under it, and the Law does not say what holds in any other case"
-- Art 10(1) (src:103-105) [J-01, J-02]: Law amended under Art 10(1); a document that is not legislation, free, technical, aimed at specialists.
#ASSERT `Can this technical document be incorporated by reference?` TRUE (`ind: a document with` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 10(1) (src:103) [J-03, J-04]: a document that is legislation of some jurisdiction is excluded.
#ASSERT `Can this technical document be incorporated by reference?` TRUE (`ind: a document with` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 10(1) (src:103) [J-05]: a document that is accessible only on payment.
#ASSERT `Can this technical document be incorporated by reference?` TRUE (`ind: a document with` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 10(2) (src:106) [J-06]: a document not concerned with the use of a technical product is not a technical document.
#ASSERT `Can this technical document be incorporated by reference?` TRUE (`ind: a document with` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 10(2) [J-07]: a document aimed at the general public is not a technical document (both limbs needed).
#ASSERT `Can this technical document be incorporated by reference?` TRUE (`ind: a document with` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 10(1) [J-09]: the Law giving the power has not been amended by Regulations under Art 10(1): the Law does not say.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Can this technical document be incorporated by reference?` FALSE (`ind: a document with` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)

§ `Article 11: annulment by the States`

-- Art 11(3) (src:112) [K-01, K-07]: an Order (one that provides for commencement and other things too) is subordinate legislation not made by the States: Art 11 applies.
#ASSERT `Does Article 11 apply to this instrument?` `an Order` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 11(3) [K-06]: an Order providing purely for commencement: Art 11 does not apply.
#ASSERT `Does Article 11 apply to this instrument?` `an Order` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 11(3) [K-05]: Regulations are made by the States: Art 11 does not apply.
#ASSERT `Does Article 11 apply to this instrument?` `Regulations` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 11(3) [K-05]: Triennial Regulations.
#ASSERT `Does Article 11 apply to this instrument?` `Triennial Regulations` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 11(3) [K-08]: an Act of the States that is Jersey legislation is made by the States.
#ASSERT `Does Article 11 apply to this instrument?` `an Act of the States that is Jersey legislation` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 11(3) [K-13]: a Law is not subordinate legislation.
#ASSERT `Does Article 11 apply to this instrument?` `a Law` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 11(3) [K-09]: another instrument having legislative effect in Jersey, not made by the States.
#ASSERT `Does Article 11 apply to this instrument?` `another instrument having legislative effect in Jersey` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 11(1) (src:108) [K-01]: an Order laid as soon as practicable: the duty is met.
#ASSERT `Has the duty to lay this instrument before the States been met?` `an Order` FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 11(1) [K-01]: an Order not laid as soon as practicable: the duty is not met.
#ASSERT `Has the duty to lay this instrument before the States been met?` `an Order` FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 11(1) (src:108) [K-01]: an Order made 1 Mar 2022, annulled at the 1st sitting after laying; the absurd 99 for the sittings since 28 Sep 2021 must be ignored for an instrument made in 2022.
#ASSERT `Has this subordinate legislation ceased to have effect because the States annulled it?` `an Order` FALSE (YMD 2022 3 1) TRUE 1 99 FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 11(1) [K-02]: at the 3rd sitting after laying: no later than 3.
#ASSERT `Has this subordinate legislation ceased to have effect because the States annulled it?` `an Order` FALSE (YMD 2022 3 1) TRUE 3 99 FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 11(1) [K-03]: at the 4th sitting after laying: too late.
#ASSERT `Has this subordinate legislation ceased to have effect because the States annulled it?` `an Order` FALSE (YMD 2022 3 1) TRUE 4 0 FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 11(1) [K-03]: at the 4th sitting after laying, the figure since 28 Sep 2021 notwithstanding.
#ASSERT `Has this subordinate legislation ceased to have effect because the States annulled it?` `an Order` FALSE (YMD 2022 3 1) TRUE 4 99 FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 11(1) [K-01]: no resolution to annul: not ceased.
#ASSERT `Has this subordinate legislation ceased to have effect because the States annulled it?` `an Order` FALSE (YMD 2022 3 1) FALSE 1 1 FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 11(2)(a) (src:110) [K-10]: the empowering Law displaces paragraph (1): the Law does not say what holds.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Has this subordinate legislation ceased to have effect because the States annulled it?` `an Order` FALSE (YMD 2022 3 1) TRUE 1 1 TRUE
-- Art 11(3) [K-05]: Regulations: Art 11 does not apply; the Law says nothing of a resolution to annul them.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Has this subordinate legislation ceased to have effect because the States annulled it?` `Regulations` FALSE (YMD 2022 3 1) TRUE 1 1 FALSE
-- Art 11(3) [K-06]: an Order providing purely for commencement: Art 11 does not apply.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Has this subordinate legislation ceased to have effect because the States annulled it?` `an Order` TRUE (YMD 2022 3 1) TRUE 1 1 FALSE
-- Art 11(2)(b) (src:111) [K-11, K-12]: annulment leaves alone what was done, and the maker's power to make further legislation.
#ASSERT `Does annulment leave alone what was done under the instrument and the power to make further legislation?` TRUE EQUALS TRUE

§ `Articles 12 to 14: consolidated legislation and editorial changes`

-- Art 12(2) (src:121) [L-01]: the text of the legislation as originally made.
#ASSERT `Is this text as-enacted legislation?` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 12(2) [L-02]: that legislation in the form it appears when prepared for publication under Part 3.
#ASSERT `Is this text as-enacted legislation?` FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 12(2) [L-01]: neither: not as-enacted legislation.
#ASSERT `Is this text as-enacted legislation?` FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 12(3) (src:122) [L-03]: modifications to show the legislation as in force on a stated date: consolidated.
#ASSERT `Is this text consolidated legislation?` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 12(4) (src:123) [L-05]: revised legislation is consolidated legislation.
#ASSERT `Is this text consolidated legislation?` FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 12(3), 12(4) [L-03]: neither.
#ASSERT `Is this text consolidated legislation?` FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 13(1) (src:125) [L-07, L-11]: Jersey legislation commenced on 29 Sep 2021, not only amending or commencing: a consolidated version is required.
#ASSERT `Does Article 13(1) require a consolidated version of this legislation to be prepared?` TRUE FALSE `the legislation is commenced` (YMD 2021 9 29) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 13(1) [L-08]: amended after Part 3 commenced.
#ASSERT `Does Article 13(1) require a consolidated version of this legislation to be prepared?` TRUE FALSE `the legislation is amended` (YMD 2022 3 1) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 13(1) [L-09]: revised after Part 3 commenced.
#ASSERT `Does Article 13(1) require a consolidated version of this legislation to be prepared?` TRUE FALSE `the legislation is revised` (YMD 2024 1 11) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 13(1) [L-10]: commenced on 27 Sep 2021, before Part 3 commenced: no duty.
#ASSERT `Does Article 13(1) require a consolidated version of this legislation to be prepared?` TRUE FALSE `the legislation is commenced` (YMD 2021 9 27) EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 13(1) [L-13, L-14, L-15]: legislation only amending or commencing other legislation, or an Act referred to in Art 2(2): no duty.
#ASSERT `Does Article 13(1) require a consolidated version of this legislation to be prepared?` TRUE TRUE `the legislation is commenced` (YMD 2022 3 1) EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 13(1) [L-16]: legislation that amends other legislation and also does something else: duty.
#ASSERT `Does Article 13(1) require a consolidated version of this legislation to be prepared?` TRUE FALSE `the legislation is amended` (YMD 2023 5 5) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 13(1) (src:125) [V-08]: UK extended legislation is not "Jersey legislation": no duty under Art 13(1).
#ASSERT `Does Article 13(1) require a consolidated version of this legislation to be prepared?` FALSE FALSE `the legislation is commenced` (YMD 2022 3 1) EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 13(1) [V-09]: none of the three events has happened.
#ASSERT `Does Article 13(1) require a consolidated version of this legislation to be prepared?` TRUE FALSE `none of these has happened` (YMD 2022 3 1) EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 13(2) (src:126) [L-18]: a consolidated text with the statement that it is consolidated legislation compiled under the authority of the Law.
#ASSERT `Does this consolidated legislation carry the statement the Law requires?` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 13(2) [L-18]: a consolidated text without it fails the requirement.
#ASSERT `Does this consolidated legislation carry the statement the Law requires?` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 14(1)(a) (src:129) [L-20]: removal of a provision relating to commencement, in consolidated legislation.
#ASSERT `May the Principal Legislative Drafter make this editorial change?` `the removal of a provision relating to its commencement` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 14(1)(b) (src:130) [L-21]: removal of a provision that amends or repeals other legislation.
#ASSERT `May the Principal Legislative Drafter make this editorial change?` `the removal of a provision that amends or repeals other legislation` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 14(1)(c) (src:131) [L-22]: removal of a provision the Drafter considers spent.
#ASSERT `May the Principal Legislative Drafter make this editorial change?` `the removal of another provision that the Principal Legislative Drafter considers spent or no longer operative` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 14(1)(d)(i) (src:133) [L-23]: typographical and clerical errors.
#ASSERT `May the Principal Legislative Drafter make this editorial change?` `the correction of typographical and clerical errors` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 14(1)(d)(ii) (src:134) [L-24]: errors in grammar, spelling and punctuation.
#ASSERT `May the Principal Legislative Drafter make this editorial change?` `the correction of errors in grammar, spelling and punctuation` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 14(1)(d)(iii) (src:135) [L-25]: errors in numbering, cross-referencing and alphabetical ordering.
#ASSERT `May the Principal Legislative Drafter make this editorial change?` `the correction of errors in numbering, cross-referencing and alphabetical ordering` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 14(1)(d)(iv) (src:136) [L-26]: errors in, or arising out of, an amendment by other legislation.
#ASSERT `May the Principal Legislative Drafter make this editorial change?` `the correction of errors in, or arising out of, an amendment by other legislation` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 14(1)(d)(v) (src:137) [L-26]: any other errors of a similar nature.
#ASSERT `May the Principal Legislative Drafter make this editorial change?` `the correction of any other errors of a similar nature` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 14(1)(e) (src:138) [L-27]: punctuation and conjunctives to add or remove a list item.
#ASSERT `May the Principal Legislative Drafter make this editorial change?` `changes in punctuation, and the relocation of conjunctives or disjunctives, to add or remove a provision in a list` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 14(1) (src:128) [V-15]: the text is not consolidated legislation: Art 14(1) gives nothing; the Law says nothing else.
#ASSERT REFUSED `May the Principal Legislative Drafter make this editorial change?` `the correction of typographical and clerical errors` FALSE BECAUSE "Article 14(1) gives the power for consolidated legislation, and the Law does not say whether the Principal Legislative Drafter may make the change in any other text"
-- Art 14(2) (src:139) [L-29]: a change that would alter the meaning of a provision does not have effect (to that extent).
#ASSERT `Does this editorial change have effect in full?` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 14(2) [L-29]: a change that would not alter the meaning has effect in full.
#ASSERT `Does this editorial change have effect in full?` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 14(3) (src:140) [L-30]: a formatting or presentational change to consolidated legislation for consistency with current drafting practice.
#ASSERT `May the Principal Legislative Drafter make this formatting or presentational change?` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 14(3) [L-30]: not made for consistency with current drafting practice: the Law says nothing.
#ASSERT REFUSED `May the Principal Legislative Drafter make this formatting or presentational change?` TRUE FALSE BECAUSE "Article 14(3) gives the power for formatting and presentational changes to consolidated legislation made so that it is consistent with current drafting practice, and the Law does not say whether the Drafter may make the change otherwise"
-- Art 14(5) (src:142) [L-31]: a change that is neither formatting nor minor editorial must be set out in an endnote or other suitable place.
#ASSERT `Must this change be set out in an endnote or other suitable place?` FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 14(5) [L-32]: a formatting or presentational change need not be.
#ASSERT `Must this change be set out in an endnote or other suitable place?` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 14(5) [L-32]: a minor editorial change need not be.
#ASSERT `Must this change be set out in an endnote or other suitable place?` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 14(6) (src:143) [L-33]: an error in a published version of as-enacted legislation that occurred after it was made.
#ASSERT `May the Principal Legislative Drafter correct this error in a published version?` `a published version of as-enacted legislation, with an error that occurred after it was made` EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 14(6) [L-35]: an error in revised legislation that occurred after its revision.
#ASSERT `May the Principal Legislative Drafter correct this error in a published version?` `a published version of revised legislation, with an error that occurred after its revision` EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 14(6) [L-34, L-36]: any other error (one in the text as originally made, or in the revision itself): Art 14(6) gives nothing.
#ASSERT REFUSED `May the Principal Legislative Drafter correct this error in a published version?` `any other published version or error` BECAUSE "Article 14(6) lets the Principal Legislative Drafter correct an error in a published version of as-enacted legislation that occurred after it was made, or of revised legislation that occurred after its revision, and the Law does not say whether the Drafter may correct any other"

§ `Article 15, Schedule 1: revision`

-- Sched 1(a) (src:228) [S-01]: citation provision, long title, short title, words of enactment or preamble.
#ASSERT `ind: Schedule 1 power relied on` `Schedule 1(a): to amend the citation provision, long title, short title, words of enactment or preamble` EQUALS TRUE
-- Sched 1(b) (src:229) [S-02]: consolidate or split legislation, or relocate a provision.
#ASSERT `ind: Schedule 1 power relied on` `Schedule 1(b): to consolidate or split legislation, or relocate a provision into different legislation` EQUALS TRUE
-- Sched 1(c) (src:230) [S-03]: rearrange provisions or a list.
#ASSERT `ind: Schedule 1 power relied on` `Schedule 1(c): to rearrange the provisions of legislation, or a list in a provision` EQUALS TRUE
-- Sched 1(d) (src:231) [S-04]: add a table of contents or destinations.
#ASSERT `ind: Schedule 1 power relied on` `Schedule 1(d): to add a table of contents or destinations` EQUALS TRUE
-- Sched 1(e) (src:232) [S-05, S-06]: add or alter a heading.
#ASSERT `ind: Schedule 1 power relied on` `Schedule 1(e): to add a heading to a provision that has none, or alter a heading` EQUALS TRUE
-- Sched 1(f) (src:233) [S-07]: omit a map, picture, drawing, diagram or other object.
#ASSERT `ind: Schedule 1 power relied on` `Schedule 1(f): to omit any map, picture, drawing, diagram or other object` EQUALS TRUE
-- Sched 1(g) (src:234) [S-08, S-09]: change a reference for a change of name or transfer of function.
#ASSERT `ind: Schedule 1 power relied on` `Schedule 1(g): to change a reference to reflect a change of name, transfer of function or provision for construction` EQUALS TRUE
-- Sched 1(h) (src:235) [S-10, S-11]: adaptations for constitutional or other changes.
#ASSERT `ind: Schedule 1 power relied on` `Schedule 1(h): to make adaptations and amendments that appear necessary or proper as a consequence of constitutional or other changes` EQUALS TRUE
-- Sched 1(i) (src:236) [S-12]: make words gender neutral.
#ASSERT `ind: Schedule 1 power relied on` `Schedule 1(i): to change words to make them gender neutral` EQUALS TRUE
-- Sched 1(j) (src:237) [S-13]: change expressions of date, money, number, time and units of measurement.
#ASSERT `ind: Schedule 1 power relied on` `Schedule 1(j): to change expressions of date, money, number, time and units of measurement` EQUALS TRUE
-- Sched 1(k) (src:238) [S-14, S-15]: delete obsolete or redundant words or provisions.
#ASSERT `ind: Schedule 1 power relied on` `Schedule 1(k): to delete obsolete or redundant words or provisions` EQUALS TRUE
-- Sched 1(l) (src:239) [S-16]: uniformity of expression.
#ASSERT `ind: Schedule 1 power relied on` `Schedule 1(l): to alter words to secure uniformity of expression` EQUALS TRUE
-- Sched 1(m) (src:240) [S-17]: shorten a phrase or sentence.
#ASSERT `ind: Schedule 1 power relied on` `Schedule 1(m): to shorten a phrase or sentence` EQUALS TRUE
-- Sched 1(n) (src:241) [S-18]: plain-language wording.
#ASSERT `ind: Schedule 1 power relied on` `Schedule 1(n): to change the wording for the better application of plain language principles` EQUALS TRUE
-- Sched 1(o) (src:242) [S-19]: add numbering or renumber.
#ASSERT `ind: Schedule 1 power relied on` `Schedule 1(o): to add numbering to, or renumber, a provision` EQUALS TRUE
-- Sched 1(p) (src:243) [S-20]: substitute a reference to the re-enacting or replacing legislation.
#ASSERT `ind: Schedule 1 power relied on` `Schedule 1(p): to substitute a reference to legislation that has been re-enacted or replaced` EQUALS TRUE
-- Sched 1(q) (src:244) [S-21, S-26]: other things the Board thinks necessary for consistency with current drafting practice.
#ASSERT `ind: Schedule 1 power relied on` `Schedule 1(q): to do all other things that appear to the Board to be necessary to render revised legislation consistent with current drafting practice` EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 15(5), 15(7) (src:155, 157) [S-24, V-04]: an Article 14 power is also a power the Board may rely on.
#ASSERT `Is the power relied on for this change one the Law gives?` (`a power in Article 14` `the correction of typographical and clerical errors`) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 15(6) (src:156) [V-01]: a draft whose only change relies on Schedule 1(k): the statement names a power for every change.
#ASSERT `Does the statement name a power for every change?` (LIST `ind: a change` "delete an obsolete word" (`a power in Schedule 1` `Schedule 1(k): to delete obsolete or redundant words or provisions`)) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 15(6) (src:156) [V-02]: a draft with one change relying on a power and one relying on none: the statement does not name a power for every change.
#ASSERT `Does the statement name a power for every change?` (LIST `ind: a change` "delete an obsolete word" (`a power in Schedule 1` `Schedule 1(k): to delete obsolete or redundant words or provisions`), `ind: a change` "rewrite a rule" `no power is stated`) EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 15(7) (src:157) [M-08]: every change relies on a power the Law gives: all within the powers.
#ASSERT `Are all the changes in this draft revision within the powers of Article 14 or Schedule 1?` (LIST `ind: a change` "delete an obsolete word" (`a power in Schedule 1` `Schedule 1(k): to delete obsolete or redundant words or provisions`), `ind: a change` "correct a typing error" (`a power in Article 14` `the correction of typographical and clerical errors`)) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 15(7) [V-03]: an empty draft: nothing outside the powers.
#ASSERT `Are all the changes in this draft revision within the powers of Article 14 or Schedule 1?` (EMPTY) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 15(7) (src:157) [M-08]: the Board is satisfied that the changes are within the powers: it may certify.
#ASSERT `May the Law Revision Board certify the draft revision as revised legislation?` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 15(7) [M-09, M-10]: the Board is not satisfied: it may certify "only if" satisfied.
#ASSERT `May the Law Revision Board certify the draft revision as revised legislation?` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 15(8) (src:158) [M-12]: a revision certified under Art 15(7): its changes have effect as if made by an amendment in other legislation.
#ASSERT `Do the changes made by a revision have effect as if made by an amendment in other legislation?` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 15(9) (src:159) [M-14]: minutes laid on the last permitted day (15 Mar 2022): in time.
#ASSERT `Did the Board lay its minutes before the States in time?` (YMD 2022 3 15) (YMD 2022 3 15) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 15(9) [M-15]: laid the day after the last permitted day.
#ASSERT `Did the Board lay its minutes before the States in time?` (YMD 2022 3 16) (YMD 2022 3 15) EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 15(9) [M-16]: laid the day before the last permitted day.
#ASSERT `Did the Board lay its minutes before the States in time?` (YMD 2022 3 14) (YMD 2022 3 15) EQUALS TRUE

§ `Article 16: publication`

-- Art 16(1)(a) (src:163) [N-01]: as-enacted legislation made on 29 Sep 2021 must be published.
#ASSERT `Does Article 16(1) require this legislation to be published?` `as-enacted legislation` (YMD 2021 9 29) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 16(1)(a) [N-02]: made on 27 Sep 2021, before Part 3 commenced.
#ASSERT `Does Article 16(1) require this legislation to be published?` `as-enacted legislation` (YMD 2021 9 27) EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 16(1)(a) [N-01]: made in 2023.
#ASSERT `Does Article 16(1) require this legislation to be published?` `as-enacted legislation` (YMD 2023 7 1) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 16(1)(b) (src:164) [N-04]: consolidated legislation prepared 2 Jan 2019 (after 1 Jan 2019).
#ASSERT `Does Article 16(1) require this legislation to be published?` `consolidated legislation` (YMD 2019 1 2) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 16(1)(b) [N-05]: prepared on 1 Jan 2019 is not "after 1st January 2019".
#ASSERT `Does Article 16(1) require this legislation to be published?` `consolidated legislation` (YMD 2019 1 1) EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 16(1)(b) [N-06]: prepared 31 Dec 2018.
#ASSERT `Does Article 16(1) require this legislation to be published?` `consolidated legislation` (YMD 2018 12 31) EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 16(1)(b) [N-07]: prepared 1 Mar 2022.
#ASSERT `Does Article 16(1) require this legislation to be published?` `consolidated legislation` (YMD 2022 3 1) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 12(4), 16(1)(b) [V-05]: revised legislation is consolidated legislation: prepared 1 Mar 2022.
#ASSERT `Does Article 16(1) require this legislation to be published?` `revised legislation` (YMD 2022 3 1) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 16(2) (src:165) [N-11]: as-enacted legislation made 5 Mar 2022: publication is due from the day it is made.
#ASSERT `From what day must this legislation be published as soon as practicable?` `as-enacted legislation` (YMD 2022 3 5) (YMD 2022 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2022 3 5
-- Art 16(2) [N-08]: consolidated 10 Mar 2022, amendments incorporated 5 Mar 2022: the later, 10 Mar.
#ASSERT `From what day must this legislation be published as soon as practicable?` `consolidated legislation` (YMD 2022 3 10) (YMD 2022 3 5) EQUALS YMD 2022 3 10
-- Art 16(2) [N-09]: consolidated 1 Mar 2022, amendments incorporated 5 Mar 2022: the later, 5 Mar.
#ASSERT `From what day must this legislation be published as soon as practicable?` `consolidated legislation` (YMD 2022 3 1) (YMD 2022 3 5) EQUALS YMD 2022 3 5
-- Art 16(2) [N-10]: both on the same day.
#ASSERT `From what day must this legislation be published as soon as practicable?` `consolidated legislation` (YMD 2022 3 7) (YMD 2022 3 7) EQUALS YMD 2022 3 7

§ `Article 17: official versions`

-- Art 17(1) (src:167) [O-01]: as-enacted legislation is an official version, with no further condition.
#ASSERT `Is this text an official version of the legislation?` (`ind: a text with` `as-enacted legislation` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 17(2)(a) (src:168-169) [O-02, O-05, O-06]: consolidated Jersey legislation with the statement, electronic version on the Drafter's website, or an unaltered printout or download of it (the same fact).
#ASSERT `Is this text an official version of the legislation?` (`ind: a text with` `consolidated legislation` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 17(2)(b) (src:170) [O-08, O-10]: with the statement, a printed version issued by or for the Drafter (needing no "without alteration", so even an altered text issued by the Drafter).
#ASSERT `Is this text an official version of the legislation?` (`ind: a text with` `consolidated legislation` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 17(2) [O-04, O-07, O-09]: with the statement, but neither an electronic version on the Drafter's website nor an unaltered copy nor a printed version issued by the Drafter.
#ASSERT `Is this text an official version of the legislation?` (`ind: a text with` `consolidated legislation` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 17(2) (src:168) [O-11]: consolidated legislation that is not Jersey legislation: paragraph (2) does not make it official.
#ASSERT `Is this text an official version of the legislation?` (`ind: a text with` `consolidated legislation` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 12(4), 17(2) [O-02]: revised legislation is consolidated legislation: with the statement and the website version, official.
#ASSERT `Is this text an official version of the legislation?` (`ind: a text with` `revised legislation` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 17(3) (src:171) [O-13]: an official version of as-enacted legislation is taken to set out its text correctly.
#ASSERT `Is the official version taken to set out the text of the as-enacted legislation correctly?` (`ind: a text with` `as-enacted legislation` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 17(4) (src:172) [O-15]: official consolidated version, asked as at the date it is stated to be consolidated, no contrary shown.
#ASSERT `Is the official version taken to set out the consolidated legislation correctly?` (`ind: a text with` `consolidated legislation` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 17(4) [O-16]: the contrary is shown.
#ASSERT `Is the official version taken to set out the consolidated legislation correctly?` (`ind: a text with` `consolidated legislation` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 17(4) (src:172) [O-17]: asked as at some other date: the presumption says nothing.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Is the official version taken to set out the consolidated legislation correctly?` (`ind: a text with` `consolidated legislation` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) FALSE FALSE
-- Art 17(4) [O-17]: a consolidated text that is not an official version: the presumption is for an official version only.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Is the official version taken to set out the consolidated legislation correctly?` (`ind: a text with` `consolidated legislation` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE) FALSE TRUE
-- Art 17(5) (src:173) [O-18]: an official as-enacted version is admissible in evidence.
#ASSERT `Is this text admissible in evidence?` (`ind: a text with` `as-enacted legislation` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 17(5) [O-18]: an official consolidated version is admissible.
#ASSERT `Is this text admissible in evidence?` (`ind: a text with` `consolidated legislation` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 17(5) [O-20]: a text that is not an official version: this Law gives no rule on admissibility.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Is this text admissible in evidence?` (`ind: a text with` `consolidated legislation` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- Art 17(5) [O-19]: a court must take judicial notice of an official version.
#ASSERT `Must a court take judicial notice of this text?` (`ind: a text with` `as-enacted legislation` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 17(5) [O-19]: an official consolidated version.
#ASSERT `Must a court take judicial notice of this text?` (`ind: a text with` `consolidated legislation` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 17(5) [O-21]: a text that is not an official version: this Law does not say.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Must a court take judicial notice of this text?` (`ind: a text with` `consolidated legislation` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§ `Article 18: Statute Law Revision Regulations`

-- Art 18(1), 18(2)(a) (src:176-178) [P-01]: amending Jersey legislation to clarify an ambiguity.
#ASSERT `Does Article 18 give Statute Law Revision Regulations the power to make this amendment?` TRUE `the amendment is necessary or desirable to clarify an ambiguity in the legislation` EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 18(2)(b) (src:179) [P-02, P-03]: reconciling inconsistencies.
#ASSERT `Does Article 18 give Statute Law Revision Regulations the power to make this amendment?` TRUE `the amendment is necessary or desirable to reconcile inconsistencies between different provisions of the legislation, or between any of its provisions and provisions of any other Jersey legislation` EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 18(1) (src:176) [P-04]: a power in Article 14.
#ASSERT `Does Article 18 give Statute Law Revision Regulations the power to make this amendment?` TRUE `the amendment uses a power set out in Article 14` EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 18(1) [P-04]: a power in Schedule 1.
#ASSERT `Does Article 18 give Statute Law Revision Regulations the power to make this amendment?` TRUE `the amendment uses a power set out in Schedule 1` EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 18(1) [P-04]: none of these: a change of policy.
#ASSERT `Does Article 18 give Statute Law Revision Regulations the power to make this amendment?` TRUE `the amendment rests on none of these` EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 18(1) [P-05]: UK extended legislation is not "Jersey legislation".
#ASSERT `Does Article 18 give Statute Law Revision Regulations the power to make this amendment?` FALSE `the amendment is necessary or desirable to clarify an ambiguity in the legislation` EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 18(3) (src:180) [P-06]: the Bailiff's opinion is that the amendment would alter the effect of legislation and it is outside paragraphs (1) and (2): barred.
#ASSERT `Is this amendment to the proposition not barred from being lodged by Article 18(3)?` TRUE TRUE TRUE `the amendment rests on none of these` EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 18(3) [P-07]: in the Bailiff's opinion it would not alter the effect.
#ASSERT `Is this amendment to the proposition not barred from being lodged by Article 18(3)?` TRUE FALSE TRUE `the amendment rests on none of these` EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 18(3) [P-06]: it would alter the effect but is within the scope of paragraph (2).
#ASSERT `Is this amendment to the proposition not barred from being lodged by Article 18(3)?` TRUE TRUE TRUE `the amendment is necessary or desirable to clarify an ambiguity in the legislation` EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 18(3) [V-10]: the proposition is not for Regulations under Article 18: Art 18(3) does not bar the amendment.
#ASSERT `Is this amendment to the proposition not barred from being lodged by Article 18(3)?` FALSE TRUE TRUE `the amendment rests on none of these` EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 18(4) (src:181) [P-08]: Regulations may make any provision a Law could make, subject to Art 18.
#ASSERT `May Statute Law Revision Regulations make this provision?` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 18(4) [V-11]: any amendment the provision makes is outside Art 18(1) and (2): subject to Art 18, not authorised.
#ASSERT `May Statute Law Revision Regulations make this provision?` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 18(4) [V-11]: a provision a Law could not make.
#ASSERT REFUSED `May Statute Law Revision Regulations make this provision?` FALSE TRUE

§ `Article 22: privilege`

-- Art 22(1), 22(2) (src:208, 214-215) [R-01]: a Member of the States gives confidential instructions to a Legislative Drafter.
#ASSERT `Are my communications with the Legislative Drafting Office privileged?` (`ind: a provider who` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `employed, including under a contract for services, to draft legislation for the Legislative Drafting Office` `instructions to draft legislation received by the Legislative Drafting Office` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 22(2) (src:214) [R-02]: an officer working in a department established by the States.
#ASSERT `Are my communications with the Legislative Drafting Office privileged?` (`ind: a provider who` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `employed, including under a contract for services, to draft legislation for the Legislative Drafting Office` `instructions to draft legislation received by the Legislative Drafting Office` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 22(2) (src:215) [R-03]: an officer in a body, office or unit established on behalf of the States.
#ASSERT `Are my communications with the Legislative Drafting Office privileged?` (`ind: a provider who` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) `employed, including under a contract for services, to draft legislation for the Legislative Drafting Office` `instructions to draft legislation received by the Legislative Drafting Office` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 22(2) (src:213) [R-04]: "includes" is not exhaustive: someone else who gives instructions.
#ASSERT `Are my communications with the Legislative Drafting Office privileged?` (`ind: a provider who` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE) `employed, including under a contract for services, to draft legislation for the Legislative Drafting Office` `instructions to draft legislation received by the Legislative Drafting Office` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 22(2)(a) (src:211) [R-07]: instructions to draft are within "confidential communications" whether or not the person calls them confidential.
#ASSERT `Are my communications with the Legislative Drafting Office privileged?` (`ind: a provider who` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `employed, including under a contract for services, to draft legislation for the Legislative Drafting Office` `instructions to draft legislation received by the Legislative Drafting Office` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 22(2)(b) (src:212) [R-08]: an unpublished draft prepared by the Office, in the hands of the provider.
#ASSERT `Are my communications with the Legislative Drafting Office privileged?` (`ind: a provider who` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `employed, including under a contract for services, to draft legislation for the Legislative Drafting Office` `an unpublished draft of legislation prepared by or on behalf of the Legislative Drafting Office` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 1 "Legislative Drafter" (src:17), Art 22(1) [V-12]: the Principal Legislative Drafter is a Legislative Drafter.
#ASSERT `Are my communications with the Legislative Drafting Office privileged?` (`ind: a provider who` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `the Principal Legislative Drafter` `instructions to draft legislation received by the Legislative Drafting Office` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 1 "Legislative Drafter" (src:17) [A-15]: a trainee Legislative Drafter is a Legislative Drafter.
#ASSERT `Are my communications with the Legislative Drafting Office privileged?` (`ind: a provider who` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `a trainee Legislative Drafter` `instructions to draft legislation received by the Legislative Drafting Office` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 22(2)(a) (src:211) [R-04]: a communication between a client and a Legislative Drafter that relates to the subject matter of the instructions, confidential.
#ASSERT `Are my communications with the Legislative Drafting Office privileged?` (`ind: a provider who` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE) `employed, including under a contract for services, to draft legislation for the Legislative Drafting Office` `a communication between a client of the Legislative Drafting Office and a Legislative Drafter that relates to the subject matter of the instructions` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 22(1) (src:208) [R-05]: any other communication that is not confidential: the Law says nothing.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Are my communications with the Legislative Drafting Office privileged?` (`ind: a provider who` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `employed, including under a contract for services, to draft legislation for the Legislative Drafting Office` `any other communication` FALSE BECAUSE "Article 22 gives legal professional privilege to confidential communications between a provider of instructions to the Legislative Drafting Office and a Legislative Drafter, and the Law says nothing of other communications"
-- Art 22(1) [R-06]: the other party is not a Legislative Drafter: the Law says nothing.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Are my communications with the Legislative Drafting Office privileged?` (`ind: a provider who` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `none of these` `instructions to draft legislation received by the Legislative Drafting Office` TRUE BECAUSE "Article 22 gives legal professional privilege to confidential communications between a provider of instructions to the Legislative Drafting Office and a Legislative Drafter, and the Law says nothing of other communications"
-- Art 22(1) (src:208) [V-12]: any other communication that is confidential, between a provider and a Legislative Drafter.
#ASSERT `Are my communications with the Legislative Drafting Office privileged?` (`ind: a provider who` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `employed, including under a contract for services, to draft legislation for the Legislative Drafting Office` `any other communication` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 22(1) [V-12]: the person is not a provider of instructions at all: the Law says nothing.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Are my communications with the Legislative Drafting Office privileged?` (`ind: a provider who` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `employed, including under a contract for services, to draft legislation for the Legislative Drafting Office` `any other communication` TRUE BECAUSE "Article 22 gives legal professional privilege to confidential communications between a provider of instructions to the Legislative Drafting Office and a Legislative Drafter, and the Law says nothing of other communications"

§ `UNSURE: the author could not decide between two readings; each assertion states the reading the author would take`

-- UNSURE [K-04] Art 11(1) (src:108): the resolution is passed at the sitting on the very day of laying (0 sittings after it). "No later than 3 sittings after" is met by an earlier sitting. Taken: ceased.
#ASSERT `Has this subordinate legislation ceased to have effect because the States annulled it?` `an Order` FALSE (YMD 2022 3 1) TRUE 0 99 FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- UNSURE [K-15] Art 11(4), 11(1) (src:113, 108): an Order made before 28 Sep 2021. (4) speaks of "3 sittings after it is made", which (1) does not contain. A: (4) moves the start of the count to the commencement of Part 2. B: (1) stands and the count runs from laying. Taken: A (the evident purpose of (4)). Here 2 sittings since 28 Sep 2021 but 6 since laying.
#ASSERT `Has this subordinate legislation ceased to have effect because the States annulled it?` `an Order` FALSE (YMD 2021 1 1) TRUE 6 2 FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- UNSURE [K-15] Art 11(4): the same Order, 4 sittings since 28 Sep 2021 but only 1 since laying. Taken: A, too late.
#ASSERT `Has this subordinate legislation ceased to have effect because the States annulled it?` `an Order` FALSE (YMD 2021 1 1) TRUE 1 4 FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- UNSURE [I-21] Art 9(6)(b) (src:100): an Order amending registered UK extended legislation. "Legislation" includes UK extended legislation (src:16) and it is not made by the States. Taken: the literal text, authorised.
#ASSERT `Can this instrument use the incidental power of Article 9(5) to make this provision?` `an Order` (`ind: to amend` `UK extended legislation` FALSE FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- UNSURE [I-24] Art 9(6)(a)-(b) (src:99-100): an Order made under a power in another Order amending that enabling Order. Art 9(6)(a) excludes "the legislation giving the power" for Regulations only. Taken: the literal text, authorised.
#ASSERT `Can this instrument use the incidental power of Article 9(5) to make this provision?` `an Order` (`ind: to amend` `an Order` FALSE TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- UNSURE [I-26] Art 9(6) (src:98-100): an Act of the States (made by the States, not Regulations) amending a Law by the incidental power. Neither (a) nor (b) names it. Taken: the literal text, Art 9(6) does not limit it.
#ASSERT `Can this instrument use the incidental power of Article 9(5) to make this provision?` `an Act of the States that is Jersey legislation` (`ind: to amend` `a Law` FALSE FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- UNSURE [O-03] Art 17(2) (src:168): consolidated Jersey legislation on the Drafter's website without the official-version statement. (2) says "is an official version if" (sufficient, not "only if"), but (6) speaks of "the requirements". Taken: not an official version.
#ASSERT `Is this text an official version of the legislation?` (`ind: a text with` `consolidated legislation` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
-- UNSURE [V-16] Art 15(7) (src:157): a change in the draft for which no power is stated. A: not shown to be within the powers, so no. B: it might still be within them, so the Law does not say. Taken: A.
#ASSERT `Are all the changes in this draft revision within the powers of Article 14 or Schedule 1?` (LIST `ind: a change` "rewrite a rule" `no power is stated`) EQUALS FALSE
-- UNSURE [V-17] Art 15(7) (src:157): the power relied on is "none stated"; the question is whether it is a power the Law gives. Taken: no.
#ASSERT `Is the power relied on for this change one the Law gives?` `no power is stated` EQUALS FALSE
